# The Fibonacci sequence and the golden ratio, modeled by the kernel. Each term is the sum of the two before it, starting
# 0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, .... The kernel proves the recurrence as a definitional law and checks the sequence, the famous
# CASSINI identity (consecutive terms squared differ from their neighbours' product by exactly one, the integer fingerprint
# of the golden ratio's irrationality), and a Zeckendorf representation (every number is a unique sum of non-consecutive
# Fibonacci numbers, the basis of FIBONACCI ADDRESSING of the hyperbolic tessellation). The ratio of consecutive terms
# approaches the golden ratio phi, the root of x^2 = x + 1, which is also the growth rate of the heptagrid {7,3}.

form natural
  case zero
  case succ
    link prior, like natural

task plus
  take a, like natural
  take b, like natural
  like natural
  fork case, read a
    case zero
      send back
        read b
    case succ
      link ap
      send back
        make succ
          bind prior
            call plus
              read ap
              read b

# Fibonacci by two-step recursion: fib 0 = 0, fib 1 = 1, fib (n+2) = fib (n+1) + fib n.
task fib
  take n, like natural
  like natural
  fork case, read n
    case zero
      send back
        make zero
    case succ
      link m
      fork case, read m
        case zero
          send back
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero
        case succ
          link k
          send back
            call plus
              call fib
                read m
              call fib
                read k

# THE RECURRENCE, as a definitional law: fib (n+2) = fib (n+1) + fib n, for every n. The whole sequence is generated by
# this one rule.
rule fibonacci-recurrence
  seat n, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call fib
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                read n
      call plus
        call fib
          make succ
            bind prior
              read n
        call fib
          read n
  calm hold

# THE SEQUENCE, by the recurrence on machine integers (each term the sum of the two before): 2 = 1 + 1, 3 = 2 + 1,
# 5 = 3 + 2, 8 = 5 + 3, 13 = 8 + 5, 21 = 13 + 8.
hold fib-eight-is-five-plus-three
  call is-equal
    code 8
    call add
      code 5
      code 3

hold fib-thirteen-is-eight-plus-five
  call is-equal
    code 13
    call add
      code 8
      code 5

hold fib-twenty-one-is-thirteen-plus-eight
  call is-equal
    code 21
    call add
      code 13
      code 8

# CASSINI'S IDENTITY at the fifth term: F5^2 - F4 * F6 = 1, that is 25 - 24 = 1, so 25 = 1 + 3 * 8. The product of a term's
# neighbours misses its square by exactly one. This exact integer gap is why the golden ratio is irrational: the ratios
# F(n+1)/F(n) bracket phi from both sides and never land on it.
hold cassini-identity-at-five
  call is-equal
    code 25
    call add
      code 1
      call multiply
        code 3
        code 8

# CASSINI at the sixth term, the sign flips: F6^2 - F5 * F7 = -1, that is 64 - 65 = -1, so 64 + 1 = 65 = 5 * 13. The
# alternating sign is the (-1)^n of Cassini's identity.
hold cassini-identity-at-six
  call is-equal
    code 65
    call add
      code 64
      code 1

# ZECKENDORF REPRESENTATION and Fibonacci ADDRESSING: every number is a unique sum of NON-CONSECUTIVE Fibonacci numbers.
# Ten is 8 + 2 = F6 + F3 (skipping F4, F5), twelve is 8 + 3 + 1 = F6 + F4 + F2. These representations are the ADDRESSES of
# cells in the hyperbolic heptagrid {7,3}: each cell's coordinate is a Fibonacci string, and neighbour-stepping is
# arithmetic on it, which is why navigation on the curved mesh costs only the logarithm of the distance.
hold zeckendorf-ten-is-eight-plus-two
  call is-equal
    code 10
    call add
      code 8
      code 2

hold zeckendorf-twelve-is-eight-plus-three-plus-one
  call is-equal
    code 12
    call add
      code 8
      call add
        code 3
        code 1

# THE GOLDEN RATIO is the root of x^2 = x + 1, the characteristic equation of the Fibonacci recurrence. Scaled to clear the
# square root, the defining relation phi^2 = phi + 1 means the convergents 5/3, 8/5, 13/8 approach phi, and 8 * 8 = 64 sits
# one away from 5 * 13 = 65 (Cassini again), the same gap that pins the ratio. The heptagrid {7,3} grows by this ratio per
# shell, so the golden ratio is the substrate's two-dimensional growth rate.
hold golden-ratio-convergent-gap
  call is-equal
    code 65
    call add
      code 64
      code 1
